-- check/bad: A.23's exclusion, seen through ANOTHER nominal type (A.58).
--
-- `HasFn` holds a function, so §6.3.1 step 4 gives it neither derived
-- method. `IndirectFn` holds a `HasFn`, and derivation is structural and
-- recursive (§3.3) — so it can have neither either.
--
-- The exclusion walked this body's `app` ARGUMENTS and stopped there, so it
-- never looked inside `HasFn`: `a < b` compiled, and the eager pass wrote a
-- parts-less `derived compare HasFn` row it had itself refused to derive.
-- The gate is now the transitive one `Types.isEquatable` already settles,
-- with a `comparable` twin beside it (A.54).
pub type HasFn
    = HasFn (Int -> Int)


pub type IndirectFn
    = Indirect HasFn


pub before : IndirectFn, IndirectFn -> Bool
before a b = a < b


pub same : IndirectFn, IndirectFn -> Bool
same a b = a == b
